  <div className="docs-layout"><nav className="docs-nav">{[['summary','Overview'],['architecture','Architecture'],['ai','AI & retrieval'],['evaluation','Evaluation'],['privacy','Privacy & security'],['demo','Judge walkthrough'],['roadmap','Status & roadmap']].map(([id,label])=><a key={id} href={'#'+id}>{label}<ChevronRight size={13}/></a>)}</nav><div className="docs-content">
  <section className="panel doc-section" id="summary"><Badge tone="green">Implemented</Badge><h2>Citizen Service Evidence & Accountability Platform</h2><p>CivicProof AI helps people prepare for Bangladesh e-Passport re-issue, compare fictional document fields, inspect official-source passages, and organize their service journey. It complements the e-Passport portal and GRS. It has no government integration or authority.</p><div className="docs-principles"><div><ShieldCheck size={23}/><h4>Evidence first</h4><p>Sources, versions, passages, and conditions remain inspectable.</p></div><div><Eye size={23}/><h4>Citizen confirmation</h4><p>Extracted fields never become confirmed without user review.</p></div><div><LockKeyhole size={23}/><h4>Synthetic by default</h4><p>No real identity documents in this demonstration.</p></div></div><p>Design inspiration: preparation checklists (UK Check and Send), case histories (USCIS), provenance (Estonia), clarification pathways (Your Europe / SOLVIT), executable conditions (Australian Rules as Code), and the distinction between uploaded and authenticated documents (DigiLocker). These are conceptual inspirations, not integrations or equivalence claims.</p><div className="button-row"><a className="text-button" href="/reports/RESEARCH.md" download>Research references<Download size={14}/></a><a className="text-button" href="/reports/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md" download>Design system<Download size={14}/></a><a className="text-button" href="/reports/screenshots/desktop-overview.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Actual interface screenshot<ArrowUpRight size={14}/></a></div></section>
- <section className="panel doc-section" id="architecture"><Badge tone="green">Implemented</Badge><h2>Architecture & data lifecycle</h2><div className="architecture"><div><Files size={20}/><strong>Synthetic file</strong><small>Browser only</small></div><ArrowRight size={16}/><div><ScanLine size={20}/><strong>Extract & confirm</strong><small>Tesseract / PDF.js</small></div><ArrowRight size={16}/><div><ListChecks size={20}/><strong>Evidence engine</strong><small>Rules + retrieval</small></div><ArrowRight size={16}/><div><GitBranch size={20}/><strong>Citizen action</strong><small>Timeline / draft</small></div></div><p>Next-compatible React 19 + TypeScript on Vinext, deployed as a Cloudflare Worker. The evidence endpoint serves a versioned source registry and deterministic evaluation. Browser sessionStorage holds only the fictional working case. Case state expires when the tab session ends; browser restore behavior can preserve a session. Use Delete all records for explicit deletion.</p><p>Original file → local OCR or PDF text extraction → editable fields → explicit confirmation → conservative comparison → source-linked finding → optional timeline record → editable clarification draft. File bytes and OCR text are not sent to the application backend. The request checker sends the fictional request text and selected conditions to the same-origin API; the API does not persist them. OCR libraries and language models download from external CDNs.</p><p>Source → version → candidate rule → confirmed field → finding → explanation → citizen action. The reviewed-rule stage remains pending specialist review. No PostgreSQL, pgvector, D1, or R2 production data store is connected. A proposed SQL migration is included for future deployment.</p></section>
+ <section className="panel doc-section" id="architecture"><Badge tone="green">Implemented</Badge><h2>Architecture & data lifecycle</h2><div className="architecture"><div><Files size={20}/><strong>Synthetic file</strong><small>Browser only</small></div><ArrowRight size={16}/><div><ScanLine size={20}/><strong>Extract & confirm</strong><small>Tesseract / PDF.js</small></div><ArrowRight size={16}/><div><ListChecks size={20}/><strong>Evidence engine</strong><small>Rules + retrieval</small></div><ArrowRight size={16}/><div><GitBranch size={20}/><strong>Citizen action</strong><small>Timeline / draft</small></div></div><p>Next.js 16 with React 19 and TypeScript. This repository targets Vercel; the original Vinext / Cloudflare build remains an optional separate deployment path. The evidence endpoint serves a versioned source registry and deterministic evaluation. Browser sessionStorage holds only the fictional working case. Case state expires when the tab session ends; browser restore behavior can preserve a session. Use Delete all records for explicit deletion.</p><p>Original file → local OCR or PDF text extraction → editable fields → explicit confirmation → conservative comparison → source-linked finding → optional timeline record → editable clarification draft. File bytes and OCR text are not sent to the application backend. The request checker sends the fictional request text and selected conditions to the same-origin API; the API does not persist them. OCR libraries and language models download from external CDNs.</p><p>Source → version → candidate rule → confirmed field → finding → explanation → citizen action. The reviewed-rule stage remains pending specialist review. No PostgreSQL, pgvector, D1, or R2 production data store is connected. A proposed SQL migration is included for future deployment.</p></section>
  <section className="panel doc-section" id="ai"><Badge tone="warning">Limited integration</Badge><h2>AI inventory, retrieval & prompts</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Actual implementation</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>OCR</td><td>Tesseract.js 5.1.1, eng + ben; local browser inference</td><td>Implemented · network-dependent</td></tr><tr><td>PDF extraction</td><td>PDF.js 4.10.38; text or first-page OCR fallback</td><td>Implemented · max 5 pages</td></tr><tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Bilingual keyword scoring over 16 clause-level mappings</td><td>Tested</td></tr><tr><td>Validation</td><td>Conditional checks, field confirmation, date validation</td><td>Tested</td></tr><tr><td>Clarification</td><td>Deterministic bilingual editable templates</td><td>Tested · no LLM</td></tr><tr><td>LLM / embeddings</td><td>No provider credentials configured</td><td>Planned</td></tr><tr><td>MCP / agents / fine-tuning</td><td>No runtime server or model training</td><td>Planned / not required for MVP</td></tr></tbody></table><p>No semantic, hybrid, graph, or agentic RAG is claimed. Retrieval has a fixed source allowlist; unknown, negated, and sensitive requests abstain. Context is bounded to four passages; deterministic checks avoid model calls. Token savings, provider cost, and model quality have not been measured.</p><p>The prompt registry includes future source-grounded extraction and explanation contracts with version identifiers and draft status. They are not presented as deployed LLM integrations. The development assistant authored the source and tests; there is no autonomous legal-rule approval.</p></section>
  <section className="panel doc-section" id="evaluation"><Badge tone={evalReport?'green':'neutral'}>{evalReport?'Tested':'Report loading'}</Badge><h2>Reproducible synthetic evaluation</h2>{evalReport?<><div className="evaluation-stats"><div><strong>{evalReport.passed}/{evalReport.total}</strong><span>Synthetic benchmark assertions</span></div><div><strong>{evalReport.metrics.mismatchPrecision}</strong><span>Mismatch precision</span></div><div><strong>{evalReport.metrics.mismatchRecall}</strong><span>Mismatch recall</span></div><div><strong>{evalReport.metrics.abstentionRate}</strong><span>Unknown-request abstention</span></div></div><p>Run: <code>node tests/evaluate.mjs</code>. Date: {evalReport.runDate}. Labels are developer-generated; this is not external legal or OCR validation. This benchmark covers field consistency, conditional mappings, unknown requests, and noisy text parsing. Raw-image OCR accuracy and language-specific OCR quality are not measured by these cases.</p><a className="text-button" href="/reports/evaluation.json" download>Download actual results<Download size={14}/></a></>:<p>No evaluation metrics are shown until the generated report is available.</p>}<p>Known retrieval limitation: keyword overlap is insufficient to establish that a complex or compound request is fully supported. All results are provisional preparation guidance. The baseline compares exact case-sensitive strings; normalized comparison handles spacing, case, and Bangla digits without fuzzy identity matching.</p></section>
  <section className="panel doc-section" id="privacy"><Badge tone="green">Implemented</Badge><h2>Privacy, safety & review boundaries</h2><ul><li>Watermarked synthetic-only file extraction; MIME, signature, file size, text-length and page-count checks.</li><li>No government impersonation, complaint submission, identity authentication, or legal eligibility decisions.</li><li>React text escaping; document content is treated as data. No instructions in documents are executed.</li><li>Application records remain in this tab. Export and explicit deletion are available in Settings.</li><li>Public administrative editing is disabled. Registry changes require source-code access.</li><li>Only request text and selected circumstances reach the request-checker API. Application code does not log request bodies. Hosting infrastructure may retain operational logs.</li><li>Private hosting access is managed by Sites. This build does not claim privacy-law certification. There is no application-level distributed rate limiter yet.</li></ul></section>
